            "id": 12,
            "options": {
              "content": "## Grafana IRM Workflow\n\n### Automatic Actions (triggered by Grafana Alert)\n1. Alert fires → Grafana IRM creates incident\n2. Incident room provisioned with: host details, CVE context, threat name, CVSS score\n3. ServiceNow ticket created via REST contact point\n4. On-call engineer paged via PagerDuty / Slack\n\n### Manual Actions (SOC Analyst)\n| Step | Action |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Open incident in Grafana IRM → review correlated events |\n| 2 | Pivot to SentinelOne → isolate endpoint |\n| 3 | Pivot to Rapid7 → confirm CVE patch availability |\n| 4 | Update ServiceNow ticket with investigation notes |\n| 5 | Confirm containment → close incident |\n\n### ServiceNow Field Mapping\n| Grafana Annotation | ServiceNow Field |\n|---|---|\n| `summary` | `short_description` |\n| `host` | `cmdb_ci` (asset lookup) |\n| `severity` | `priority` (1=Critical, 2=High) |\n| `description` | `description` |\n| `runbook_url` | `work_notes` |\n\n### Enterprise Plugin Configuration\nTo connect live ServiceNow data:\n1. Install [ServiceNow datasource plugin](https://grafana.com/grafana/plugins/grafana-servicenow-datasource/)\n2. Configure instance URL + OAuth in datasource settings\n3. Replace Loki query panels with ServiceNow queries\n4. Filters: `state=1` (New), `category=Security Incident`",
              "mode": "markdown"
            },
            "title": "Grafana IRM — Incident Response Runbook",
            "type": "text"
